# Rust build output
/target/
/spike/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Machine-local Claude Code configuration (never committed)
.claude/settings.local.json

# local-rag store artifacts — canonical/rebuildable data must never be committed
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
/store/
spool/
models/
quarantine/

# ...but `crates/models` is source code (the T11-06 model-asset installer and
# ONNX provider), not a store's downloaded-weights directory. The rule above is
# deliberately path-agnostic so a store created anywhere is covered; this one
# line re-includes the crate. Weights themselves stay ignored: they only ever
# land in `<store>/models/<model_id>/`, never under `crates/`.
!/crates/models/

# Logs and local scratch
*.log
/logs/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# npm build/test artifacts (T17-01) — node_modules is never installed in the
# checkout itself; *.tgz is a stray non-dry-run `npm pack` from manual testing.
npm/**/node_modules/
npm/**/*.tgz

# Root-level node_modules: what `npm install` at the root produces from the
# committed root package.json's `file:npm/memory` link (T22-11) — a developer
# convenience only. Nothing in the product consults node_modules any more
# (ADR-0013 Decision 3), so this is never needed to run anything, and never
# committed.
/node_modules/

# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS committed (workspace with binaries / dependency policy).

AGENTS.md
